INSERT INTO `modules_informations` VALUES
(1,'centreon-license-manager','Centreon License Manager','25.10.6','1','The Centreon IT or Business Editions require a software license or on-line subscription. This module is mandatory to validate them. This also applies to registering a platform to a free Centreon account to get extra Monitoring Connectors.','Centreon',NULL,NULL),
(2,'centreon-pp-manager','Centreon Monitoring Connector Manager','25.10.5','1','The Centreon Monitoring Connector Manager module allows to manage monitoring templates and discovery rules from the Centreon connectors catalog. By installing connectors and following their associated monitoring procedure, you will easily and quickly monitor more than 300 IT domains (Cloud infrastructure, on promise equipment, applications, etc.).\nCoupled to Centreon Auto Discovery module, you will be assist to add your Cloud infrastructure into Centreon and keep up to date your monitoring configuration.\n','Centreon',NULL,NULL),
(3,'centreon-autodiscovery-server','Centreon Auto Discovery','25.10.6','1','The Centreon Auto Discovery module discovers resources to be monitored and manually or automatically configures them in Centreon.\n\nResources can be hosts discovered from an external source or from a local subnet for examples, or services discovered from a host.\n\nHost Discovery\n\nThrough a wizard, choosing a Provider, the user can discover hosts and add them to the configuration.\n\nJobs can be scheduled to launch discovery, process the result and add hosts automatically.\n\nService Discovery\n\nTwo modes are available. The first mode provides access to a menu to manually select a host, a rule of discovery and discover the available items to monitor. The user has the choice to select items and add them to monitoring.\n\nThe second mode uses a cron job. The cron job retrieves the list of all activated discovery rules and executes them. If a new item is found when analysing a host’s content, a new service is created to monitor it. If a known element is not present anymore, the associated service is disabled.\n\nRegardless the actions is being done by the process (creation/deactivation of service), the contacts associated to discovery rules will be notified about changes. Once the process is done, the monitoring engine configuration will be updated and this one restarted.\n','Centreon',NULL,NULL),
(4,'centreon-it-edition-extensions','Centreon IT Edition Extensions','25.10.6','1','The Centreon IT or Business Editions require a software license or on-line subscription. This module is mandatory to validate them. This also applies to registering a platform to a free Centreon account to get extra Monitoring Connectors.','Centreon',NULL,NULL);
